  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), **two consecutive pages of one public topic, fetched without cookies**. The corpus has pages 1, 1100, 2201 and 2202 of topic 28563 (`R20`, `R22a`, `R22b`, `R24`), but no consecutive pair. So LOT-093's filtered-posts walk is never tested through two successfully read pages: the accumulated batch, the progress for each page, the continuation block that opens the second page.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Topic 28563 (the corpus topic) or any public topic: pages *N* and *N + 1*, both anonymous GETs of `forum2.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=<cat>&post=<post>&page=<n>`, with their redirects in the meta, as for `R22a`.\n- A read-only GET only. No write and no session.\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field: pseudos → `user1`/`user2`/`userN`, ids → `9000NN`. Never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36). One PR per batch of captures.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-093 (#185, filtered posts, PR #349): a test of the page walk over two read pages, requested by CodeRabbit on #349.\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\nLOT-093 spec, \"Pending capture\" (PR #349).\n",
